+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Services need to change stored and exchanged JSON documents with the standard patch format (RFC 6902) rather than ad-hoc update code. The library already resolves RFC 6901 pointers, which JSON Patch builds on.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, implementing the six RFC 6902 operations: `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test`.
+- It returns the patched document as a new value and never mutates its input (nor shares structure with the patch's values).
+- It throws when the patch is malformed or any operation fails; no partial result is returned.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: Applying RFC 6902 JSON Patch documents to JSON documents.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New module `src/json-patch.ts`, re-exported from `src/index.ts`; new tests in `test/`.
+- Reuses the pointer parsing of `src/json-pointer.ts`. No new dependencies; no existing behavior changes.
