+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+Apply RFC 6902 JSON Patch documents to JSON documents, so services share one standard way to express and perform updates.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Apply a patch without mutation
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` SHALL apply the operations of `patch`, an array, in order, each to the result of the previous one, and return the resulting document. It SHALL NOT mutate `document` or `patch`, and the returned document SHALL NOT share any object or array with either of them. An empty patch returns a document equal to the input. If any operation fails, an error SHALL be thrown and no result returned.
+
+#### Scenario: Input untouched
+- **WHEN** a patch with `add`, `remove` and `replace` operations is applied to a document
+- **THEN** the original document and patch are unchanged, deeply equal to before
+
+#### Scenario: Operations in order
+- **WHEN** the document is `{}` and the patch is `[{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":1},{"op":"replace","path":"/a","value":2}]`
+- **THEN** `{"a":2}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: No aliasing with patch values
+- **WHEN** an `add` value is an object and the result is later modified
+- **THEN** the patch's value is not affected
+
+#### Scenario: Failure is an error
+- **WHEN** the second of two operations fails
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: Reject invalid patches
+`applyPatch` SHALL throw an error when `patch` is not an array; when an operation is not an object; when `op` is missing or is not one of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test`; when `path` is missing or not a valid JSON Pointer string; when `add`, `replace` or `test` lacks a `value` member (a `value` of `null` is valid); or when `move` or `copy` lacks a `from` that is a valid JSON Pointer string. Members not defined by the operation SHALL be ignored.
+
+#### Scenario: Malformed patches
+- **WHEN** the patch is `{}`, `[1]`, `[{"path":"/a"}]`, `[{"op":"bogus","path":"/a"}]`, `[{"op":"add","path":"/a"}]`, `[{"op":"remove"}]`, `[{"op":"move","path":"/a"}]` or `[{"op":"add","path":"a","value":1}]`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Null value
+- **WHEN** the patch is `[{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":null}]` on `{}`
+- **THEN** `{"a":null}` is returned
+
+### Requirement: add
+`add` SHALL set the value at `path`. With an empty `path` it replaces the whole document. When the parent is an object, it adds the member or replaces an existing one. When the parent is an array, the final token SHALL be an index from `0` to the array length, inserting before that index and shifting later elements, or `-`, appending. The parent of the target SHALL exist; otherwise an error is thrown. An index beyond the length, or a non-canonical index, SHALL cause an error.
+
+#### Scenario: Add and replace object member
+- **WHEN** `{"a":1}` is patched with `add /b 2` and `add /a 3`
+- **THEN** `{"a":3,"b":2}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Insert into array
+- **WHEN** `["a","c"]` is patched with `add /1 "b"`
+- **THEN** `["a","b","c"]` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Append to array
+- **WHEN** `[1]` is patched with `add /- 2` or `add /1 2`
+- **THEN** `[1,2]` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Replace whole document
+- **WHEN** the path is `""` and the value is `[1]`
+- **THEN** `[1]` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Add failures
+- **WHEN** `[1]` is patched with `add /3 0`, `add /01 0` or `add /x 0`, or `{}` with `add /a/b 1`, or a primitive's child
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Special member names
+- **WHEN** `{}` is patched with `add /__proto__ 1`
+- **THEN** the result has an own member `__proto__` equal to `1`, and no prototype is altered
+
+### Requirement: remove
+`remove` SHALL delete the value at `path`, which SHALL exist. Removing an array element shifts later elements down. Array index `-` is an error. Removing with an empty `path` SHALL cause an error, since the whole document cannot be removed.
+
+#### Scenario: Remove member and element
+- **WHEN** `{"a":1,"b":[1,2,3]}` is patched with `remove /a` and `remove /b/1`
+- **THEN** `{"b":[1,3]}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Remove missing target
+- **WHEN** `{}` is patched with `remove /a`, or `[1]` with `remove /1` or `remove /-`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: replace
+`replace` SHALL set the value at `path`, which SHALL already exist, otherwise an error is thrown. An empty `path` replaces the whole document. Index `-` is an error.
+
+#### Scenario: Replace
+- **WHEN** `{"a":1}` is patched with `replace /a 2`
+- **THEN** `{"a":2}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Replace missing target
+- **WHEN** `{}` is patched with `replace /a 1`, or `[1]` with `replace /1 2`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: move
+`move` SHALL remove the value at `from`, which SHALL exist, and add it at `path`, as `remove` followed by `add`. A `from` that is a proper prefix of `path` (moving a value into one of its own children) SHALL cause an error. Moving a location to itself leaves the document unchanged.
+
+#### Scenario: Move member
+- **WHEN** `{"a":{"b":1},"c":2}` is patched with `move /a/b -> /d`
+- **THEN** `{"a":{},"c":2,"d":1}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Move within array
+- **WHEN** `["a","b","c"]` is patched with `move /0 -> /2`
+- **THEN** `["b","c","a"]` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Move into own child
+- **WHEN** `{"a":{}}` is patched with `move /a -> /a/b`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Move from missing location
+- **WHEN** `from` does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: copy
+`copy` SHALL add a deep copy of the value at `from`, which SHALL exist, at `path`, with the semantics of `add`. Later changes to one copy SHALL NOT affect the other.
+
+#### Scenario: Copy
+- **WHEN** `{"a":{"x":1}}` is patched with `copy /a -> /b` then `add /b/y 2`
+- **THEN** `{"a":{"x":1},"b":{"x":1,"y":2}}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Copy from missing location
+- **WHEN** `from` does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: test
+`test` SHALL succeed, leaving the document unchanged, only if the value at `path`, which SHALL exist, equals `value` by JSON equality; otherwise an error is thrown. Equality: same type; strings and booleans and `null` by value; numbers by numeric value; arrays of the same length with equal elements in order; objects with the same set of member names and equal values, regardless of member order. Whether `path` is missing or the values differ, an error is thrown.
+
+#### Scenario: Equal values
+- **WHEN** `{"a":{"x":[1,{"y":null}],"z":"s"}}` is tested at `/a` against `{"z":"s","x":[1,{"y":null}]}`
+- **THEN** the patch succeeds
+
+#### Scenario: Unequal values
+- **WHEN** a test compares `1` with `"1"`, `[1,2]` with `[2,1]`, `{"a":1}` with `{"a":1,"b":2}`, `0` with `null`, or `{}` with `[]`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Test on missing path
+- **WHEN** the path does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Test aborts patch
+- **WHEN** a failing `test` precedes an `add`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and no result is returned
